{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In order to allow individual test methods to be executed in isolation and to avoid unexpected side effects due to mutable test instance state, JUnit creates a new instance of each test class before executing each "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "test method"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (see "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "writing-tests/definitions.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "writing-tests/definitions.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). This \"per-method\" test instance lifecycle is the default behavior in JUnit Jupiter and is analogous to all previous versions of JUnit."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Please note that the test class will still be instantiated if a given "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "test method"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "disabled"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " via a "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "condition"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "writing-tests/conditional-test-execution.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@Disabled"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@DisabledOnOs"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", etc.) even when the \"per-method\" test instance lifecycle mode is active."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you would prefer that JUnit Jupiter execute all test methods on the same test instance, annotate your test class with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@TestInstance(Lifecycle.PER_CLASS)"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". When using this mode, a new test instance will be created once per test class. Thus, if your test methods rely on state stored in instance variables, you may need to reset that state in "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@BeforeEach"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@AfterEach"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The \"per-class\" mode has some additional benefits over the default \"per-method\" mode. Specifically, with the \"per-class\" mode it becomes possible to declare "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@BeforeAll"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@AfterAll"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " on non-static methods as well as on interface "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "default"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " methods."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you are authoring tests using the Kotlin programming language, you may also find it easier to implement non-static "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@BeforeAll"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@AfterAll"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " lifecycle methods as well as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@MethodSource"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " factory methods by switching to the \"per-class\" test instance lifecycle mode."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If a test class or test interface is not annotated with "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "@TestInstance"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", JUnit Jupiter will use a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "default"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " lifecycle mode. The standard "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "default"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " mode is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "PER_METHOD"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "; however, it is possible to change the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "default"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for the execution of an entire test plan. To change the default test instance lifecycle mode, set the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "junit.jupiter.testinstance.lifecycle.default"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "configuration parameter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to the name of an enum constant defined in "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "TestInstance.Lifecycle"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", ignoring case. This can be supplied as a JVM system property, as a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "configuration parameter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "LauncherDiscoveryRequest"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " that is passed to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Launcher"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", or via the JUnit Platform configuration file (see "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "running-tests/configuration-parameters.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "running-tests/configuration-parameters.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " for details)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "For example, to set the default test instance lifecycle mode to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Lifecycle.PER_CLASS"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", you can start your JVM with the following system property."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-Djunit.jupiter.testinstance.lifecycle.default=per_class"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note, however, that setting the default test instance lifecycle mode via the JUnit Platform configuration file is a more robust solution since the configuration file can be checked into a version control system along with your project and can therefore be used within IDEs and your build software."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To set the default test instance lifecycle mode to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Lifecycle.PER_CLASS"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " via the JUnit Platform configuration file, create a file named "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "junit-platform.properties"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in the root of the class path (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "src/test/resources"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") with the following content."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "junit.jupiter.testinstance.lifecycle.default = per_class"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Changing the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "default"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " test instance lifecycle mode can lead to unpredictable results and fragile builds if not applied consistently. For example, if the build configures \"per-class\" semantics as the default but tests in the IDE are executed using \"per-method\" semantics, that can make it difficult to debug errors that occur on the build server. It is therefore recommended to change the default in the JUnit Platform configuration file instead of via a JVM system property."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "warning"
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "default",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Changing the Default Test Instance Lifecycle"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Test Instance Lifecycle"
      }
    ]
  }
}
